    choose: [['It is good to (catch up / catch out) with old friends.', 'catch up'], ['We can pick up where we (left / leave) off.', 'left'], ['We want to pass these skills (down / away).', 'down'], ['The event could keep the craft (alive / living).', 'alive'], ['We have not all met (for / since) nearly five years.', 'for'], ['Why don’t we (ask / asking) her first?', 'ask']],
    choices: [['You want to exchange news after time apart. What fits?', 'Let’s catch up.', 'Let’s put off the conversation.', 'A'], ['What does passing a skill down involve?', 'Storing the finished work without teaching it.', 'Teaching it to a younger generation.', 'B'], ['What is a respectful first step?', 'Ask the artisan what she wants to share.', 'Promise an event before speaking to her.', 'A'], ['Does the workshop’s concern prove all young people dislike crafts?', 'Yes, her concern describes every young person.', 'No, this family is worried about its learners.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: 'You are Aiko. Your tutor is Haru. You are still at the family workshop after the reunion. Discuss the concern about younger learners and suggest a respectful first step toward an event.', task: 'Reconnect briefly, ask about the workshop, and suggest one way to invite interest without making promises for Mrs. Takeda.', roles: ['Haru', 'Aiko'], lines: ['Aiko, it has been nearly five years. How does it feel to be together again?', 'Grandmother worries about passing the skills down. What could we try?', 'Why might trying the craft help more than simply looking at it?', 'What should we ask her before making a plan?', 'Could you help us think of a first step?'], evidence: 'The event is only an idea in this episode. No budget, date, classes or committee approval exists yet. Haru’s concern is about this workshop, not a claim about all young people. Assess a relevant suggestion with a reason and a natural response. Do not demand every expression or a long speech.', useful: ['It is good to catch up ...', 'How has ... changed?', 'Why don’t we ...?', 'That might help because ...', 'We should ask ... first.'] },
